IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei3-part3-premium-rate`

-- Tests of ei3-part3-premium-rate.l4 (Act ss 65.21, 66 to 66.6).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the section named beside it, never from the rule's output.
-- Rates are fractions: 1.63% is 0.0163. Every figure here is invented for the test; none is a published premium rate.

§ `s 65.21 actuary`

-- Both limbs are needed: a Fellow of the Institute AND engaged by the Commission under s 28(4).
#ASSERT `s 65.21 actuary` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 65.21 actuary` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 65.21 actuary` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 65.21 actuary` FALSE FALSE)

§ `s 66(1) the seven-year period and the object of the rate`

-- A period that commences at the beginning of 2027 ends at the end of 2033 (seven calendar years).
#ASSERT `s 66(1) the seven-year period that commences at the beginning of the year` 2027 EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2027 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2033 12 31)
-- "Just enough" read as equal totals (fork F-ei3-1): equal is enough, one dollar apart is not, either way round.
#ASSERT `s 66(1) the premium rate generates just enough premium revenue` 5_000_000 5_000_000
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66(1) the premium rate generates just enough premium revenue` 5_000_001 5_000_000)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66(1) the premium rate generates just enough premium revenue` 5_000_000 5_000_001)

§ `s 66(2) the factors`

-- Arguments: based on (a) ss 66.1/66.2 info; (b) actuary's report; regulations exist; based on them; announcement made;
-- based on the change; Commission considers other info relevant; based on it.
#ASSERT `s 66(2) the Commission has set the premium rate on the factors the Act names` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- (d) and (e) and (f) bite only when there is something to be based on: nothing exists, nothing is required.
#ASSERT `s 66(2) the Commission has set the premium rate on the factors the Act names` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Regulations under s 69 exist but the rate is not based on them.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66(2) the Commission has set the premium rate on the factors the Act names` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- A Minister's announced change that the rate ignores.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66(2) the Commission has set the premium rate on the factors the Act names` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Other information the Commission considers relevant but the rate ignores.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66(2) the Commission has set the premium rate on the factors the Act names` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Paragraph (a) and paragraph (b) are always required.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66(2) the Commission has set the premium rate on the factors the Act names` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66(2) the Commission has set the premium rate on the factors the Act names` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `s 66(7) and (8) the limit on the change from one year to the next`

#ASSERT `s 66(7) the maximum change in the premium rate from one year to the next` EQUALS 0.0005
-- s 66(8): no Order in Council, the 0.05% stays; an Order fixing 0.10% replaces it.
#ASSERT `s 66(8) the maximum change in force` NOTHING EQUALS 0.0005
#ASSERT `s 66(8) the maximum change in force` (JUST 0.001) EQUALS 0.001
-- The Governor in Council needs both the joint recommendation and its own view that it is in the public interest.
#ASSERT `s 66(8) the Governor in Council may change the maximum percentage` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66(8) the Governor in Council may change the maximum percentage` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66(8) the Governor in Council may change the maximum percentage` FALSE TRUE)
-- Boundary: exactly 0.05% up (1.63% to 1.68%) is not more than the maximum; 0.06% up is more.
#ASSERT `s 66(7) the change is not more than the maximum` 0.0163 0.0168 0.0005
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66(7) the change is not more than the maximum` 0.0163 0.0169 0.0005)
-- Down as well as up: 1.63% to 1.58% is exactly 0.05%; to 1.57% is 0.06%.
#ASSERT `s 66(7) the change is not more than the maximum` 0.0163 0.0158 0.0005
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66(7) the change is not more than the maximum` 0.0163 0.0157 0.0005)
-- No change at all.
#ASSERT `s 66(7) the change is not more than the maximum` 0.0163 0.0163 0.0005
-- With a maximum of 0.10% fixed by the Governor in Council, a 0.10% rise is not more than the maximum.
#ASSERT `s 66(7) the change is not more than the maximum` 0.0163 0.0173 0.001
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66(7) the change is not more than the maximum` 0.0163 0.0174 0.001)
-- s 66.32(2): the limit does not apply to a rate set by the Governor in Council under s 66.32(1).
#ASSERT `s 66.32(2) subsection 66(7) applies to the setting of the premium rate` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.32(2) subsection 66(7) applies to the setting of the premium rate` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66(7) the premium rate may be set as it is` 0.0163 0.0200 0.0005 FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 66(7) the premium rate may be set as it is` 0.0163 0.0200 0.0005 TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(7) the premium rate may be set as it is` 0.0163 0.0168 0.0005 FALSE

§ `s 66(9) the Commission's time limit`

#ASSERT `s 66(9) the day on or before which the Commission shall set the premium rate for the following year` 2027 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 9 14
#ASSERT `s 66(9) the Commission set the premium rate in time` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 9 14)
#ASSERT `s 66(9) the Commission set the premium rate in time` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 8 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66(9) the Commission set the premium rate in time` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 9 15))

§ `s 66.1 the Minister's information`

#ASSERT `s 66.1(1) the day on or before which the Minister shall provide the information` 2027 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 7 22
-- Arguments: year; day provided; to actuary; to Commission; announcement made; (a) forecast change; (b) forecast costs;
-- (c) total charged; (d) prescribed information.
#ASSERT `s 66.1(1) the Minister has provided the information` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 7 22) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.1(1) the Minister has provided the information` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 7 23) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Paragraph (a) is required only after an announcement under s 66(2)(e).
#ASSERT `s 66.1(1) the Minister has provided the information` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 7 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.1(1) the Minister has provided the information` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 7 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Paragraphs (b), (c), (d) are always required, and the information goes to both the actuary and the Commission.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.1(1) the Minister has provided the information` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 7 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.1(1) the Minister has provided the information` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 7 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.1(1) the Minister has provided the information` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 7 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.1(1) the Minister has provided the information` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 7 1) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.1(1) the Minister has provided the information` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 7 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§ `s 66.2 the Minister of Finance's information`

#ASSERT `s 66.2(1) the day on or before which the Minister of Finance shall provide the information` 2027 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 7 22
-- Arguments: year; day provided; to actuary; to Commission; (a) economic variables; (b) the s 77.1 amounts; (c) prescribed.
#ASSERT `s 66.2(1) the Minister of Finance has provided the information` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 7 22) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.2(1) the Minister of Finance has provided the information` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 7 23) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.2(1) the Minister of Finance has provided the information` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 7 1) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.2(1) the Minister of Finance has provided the information` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 7 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.2(1) the Minister of Finance has provided the information` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 7 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.2(1) the Minister of Finance has provided the information` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 7 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.2(1) the Minister of Finance has provided the information` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 7 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§ `s 66.3 the actuary's report`

#ASSERT `s 66.3 the day on or before which the actuary shall provide the report` 2027 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 8 22
-- Arguments: year; day provided; (a) forecast rate and analysis; (b) calculations for ss 4 and 69; (c) s 66.1 information; (d) sources.
#ASSERT `s 66.3 the actuary has provided the report` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 8 22) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.3 the actuary has provided the report` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 8 23) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.3 the actuary has provided the report` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 8 1) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.3 the actuary has provided the report` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 8 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.3 the actuary has provided the report` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 8 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.3 the actuary has provided the report` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 8 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§ `s 66.31 report, public, Parliament`

#ASSERT `s 66.31(1) the day on or before which the Commission shall provide the report and summary` 2027 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 8 31
#ASSERT `s 66.31(1) the Commission has provided the report and summary` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 8 31) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.31(1) the Commission has provided the report and summary` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 9 1) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.31(1) the Commission has provided the report and summary` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 8 1) FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.31(1) the Commission has provided the report and summary` 2027 (YearMonthDay 2027 8 1) TRUE FALSE)
-- s 66.31(2): on the day the rate is set, neither earlier nor later.
#ASSERT `s 66.31(2) the Commission has made the report and summary available to the public in time` (YearMonthDay 2027 9 14) (YearMonthDay 2027 9 14)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.31(2) the Commission has made the report and summary available to the public in time` (YearMonthDay 2027 9 14) (YearMonthDay 2027 9 15))
-- s 66.31(3): "any of the next 10 days during which that House is sitting": sitting days 1 to 10.
#ASSERT `s 66.31(3) the report and summary were laid before a House in time` 1
#ASSERT `s 66.31(3) the report and summary were laid before a House in time` 10
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.31(3) the report and summary were laid before a House in time` 0)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.31(3) the report and summary were laid before a House in time` 11)
#ASSERT `s 66.31(3) the report and summary were laid before each House of Parliament in time` 3 10
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.31(3) the report and summary were laid before each House of Parliament in time` 3 11)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.31(3) the report and summary were laid before each House of Parliament in time` 11 3)

§ `s 66.32 the Governor in Council`

-- (1)(a) arguments: year; joint recommendation; public interest; day of the order; substituted rate; the Commission's rate.
#ASSERT `s 66.32(1)(a) the Governor in Council may substitute a premium rate` 2027 TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 9 30) 0.0170 0.0163
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.32(1)(a) the Governor in Council may substitute a premium rate` 2027 TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 10 1) 0.0170 0.0163)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.32(1)(a) the Governor in Council may substitute a premium rate` 2027 FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 9 20) 0.0170 0.0163)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.32(1)(a) the Governor in Council may substitute a premium rate` 2027 TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2027 9 20) 0.0170 0.0163)
-- "Different from the one set by the Commission": the same rate is not a substitution.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.32(1)(a) the Governor in Council may substitute a premium rate` 2027 TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 9 20) 0.0163 0.0163)
-- (1)(b) arguments: year; joint recommendation; day of the order; the day the Commission set a rate, if it did.
#ASSERT `s 66.32(1)(b) the Governor in Council may set the premium rate` 2027 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 9 30) NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 66.32(1)(b) the Governor in Council may set the premium rate` 2027 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 9 20) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2027 9 15))
-- A rate the Commission set on September 14 is in time, so the Governor in Council may not set one.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.32(1)(b) the Governor in Council may set the premium rate` 2027 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 9 20) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2027 9 14)))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.32(1)(b) the Governor in Council may set the premium rate` 2027 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 10 1) NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.32(1)(b) the Governor in Council may set the premium rate` 2027 FALSE (YearMonthDay 2027 9 20) NOTHING)

§ `ss 66.4 to 66.6 rounding, publication, Service Fees Act`

-- s 66.4: to the nearest 0.01%, the higher when equidistant. 1.6349% is below the midpoint of 1.63% and 1.64%;
-- 1.635% is the midpoint (the higher, 1.64%); 1.6351% is above it; 1.625% is the midpoint of 1.62% and 1.63%.
#ASSERT `s 66.4 the premium rate rounded to the nearest one hundredth of one per cent` 0.016349 EQUALS 0.0163
#ASSERT `s 66.4 the premium rate rounded to the nearest one hundredth of one per cent` 0.01635 EQUALS 0.0164
#ASSERT `s 66.4 the premium rate rounded to the nearest one hundredth of one per cent` 0.016351 EQUALS 0.0164
#ASSERT `s 66.4 the premium rate rounded to the nearest one hundredth of one per cent` 0.01625 EQUALS 0.0163
-- A rate with no fraction of one per cent, and one already at two decimals of a per cent, are left alone.
#ASSERT `s 66.4 the premium rate rounded to the nearest one hundredth of one per cent` 0.02 EQUALS 0.02
#ASSERT `s 66.4 the premium rate rounded to the nearest one hundredth of one per cent` 0.0163 EQUALS 0.0163
-- s 66.5: both the Part I publication and the speed.
#ASSERT `s 66.5 the Commission has published the premium rate as required` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.5 the Commission has published the premium rate as required` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 66.5 the Commission has published the premium rate as required` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 66.6: the Act says the Service Fees Act does not apply to these; for anything else it says nothing (not covered).
#ASSERT `s 66.6 the Service Fees Act applies` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66.6 the Service Fees Act applies` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
